        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275">

                <pb facs="0721" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg635"/>

                <head>No. 272.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bliss to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 3, 1872</date>.
                        (Received December 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 683.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The great events of the past month have
                    been the declaration of the election of Mr. Lerdo to the presidency, and his
                    inauguration on the 1st instant, which form the subject of a separate dispatch.
                    The unanimity with which Mr. Lerdo has been chosen is without a precedent in
                    Mexican annals, and the nation now entertains the brightest hopes of the
                    preservation of peace and the consequent immense development of the resources of
                    the country.</p>
                <p>General Porfirio Diaz arrived in this capital on the 17th ultimo, from Chihuahua.
                    He is living in the closest retirement, and is indisposed to take any further
                    part in politics.</p>
                <p>Congress has issued a summons for the election of a chief justice and two
                    associate justices of the supreme court, on the second and fourth <pb
                        facs="0722" n="636" xml:id="pg636"/> Sundays of February next. The contest
                    for the first-named post, which is virtually the vice-presidency of the
                    republic, has already commenced, and will be severe. The candidates so far are
                    Generals Miguel Anza and Vicente Riva Palacio, and Mr. José Maria Iglesias, all
                    of whom are friends of Mr. Lerdo.</p>
                <p>The railway project of General Rosecrans was on the 29th ultimo, after a long and
                    exhausting debate of two months, submitted to President Lerdo, with power to
                    negotiate with that gentleman, subject to the ratification of Congress.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PORTER C. BLISS.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
